#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:2
msgid "General Mattermost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:5
msgid "Why was Mattermost created?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost was created to offer an alternative to proprietary SaaS "
"services. For more information, please see the article `Why we built "
"Mattermost <https://mattermost.com/about-us/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:10
msgid ""
"Why does the open source repository contain code specific to the "
"commercial version of Mattermost?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:12
msgid ""
"The :ref:`commercial version of Mattermost <product-overview/editions-"
"and-offerings:mattermost enterprise edition>` is designed to never lock-"
"in your data. Portions of the commercial version are shared with the "
":ref:`open source version <product-overview/editions-and-"
"offerings:mattermost team edition>` to ensure upgrade and downgrade "
"across editions happens without data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:15
msgid "Does Mattermost support 508 Compliance?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:17
msgid ""
"Yes. See the :doc:`accessibility compliance policy </product-overview"
"/accessibility-compliance-policy>` documentation for details. Mattermost "
"Enterprise Edition has been purchased by multiple US public sector "
"organizations, including US federal agencies and the Department of "
"Defense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:20
msgid "What's the largest Mattermost deployment you have?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:22
msgid ""
"Our largest contractual obligation is for over a quarter of a million "
"registered users. Our most typical large enterprise deployment size is "
"between 10,000 and 40,000 users in Dev and Ops organizations who use "
"Mattermost for DevOps workflows, remote work, mission-critical and rapid "
"response, and to address email overload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:24
msgid ""
"We have done performance testing of 60,000 concurrent users and 60 "
"million posts in the database, with a peak concurrent utilization safety "
"factor of between 10 to 1 and 3 to 1, depending on the distribution of an"
" organization across time zones. Peak concurrent usage in a single "
"timezone is generally around the start of the day, probably 9am, and "
"lunchtime when people are messaging to meet for a meal. Our monthly "
"releases are tested at 20 million posts in the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:26
msgid ""
"Mattermost provides an open source, well-documented `load test simulator "
"<https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost-load-test>`__ to verify that "
"your Mattermost deployment can achieve the stated scale benchmarks ahead "
"of production deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:29
msgid ""
"What happens if I have more than 10,000 messages in my database and have "
"upgraded to Entry?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:31
msgid ""
"Entry limits the number of messages shown in the end user inteface for "
"channel history and search. All records are retained in the database. "
"Upgrading to a paid version of Mattermost will unlock this and other "
"Entry limitations. Migrating to Team Edition will also unlock full "
"history of channels, but will limit what features are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:34
msgid "What are the limitations for embargoed countries?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:36
msgid ""
"We greatly appreciate your interest in Mattermost. Due to recent "
"sanctions from the United States government, we must pause interactions "
"with your organization until the sanctions are lifted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:38
msgid "This includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:40
msgid ""
"We must pause on selling, issuing, or renewing a Mattermost license key "
"to your organization. If you have a Mattermost license key, or a trial "
"key, we ask that you do not use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:41
msgid ""
"We are not permitted to provide you technical support for our software. "
"Moreover, we cannot answer questions about our software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:42
msgid ""
"We are not permitted to provide our software, including any updates, "
"upgrades or cloud-hosted versions to your organization. We must ask that "
"you do not use any software or online services provided by Mattermost, "
"Inc., including any versions that have been provided online to the "
"general public."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:44
msgid ""
"We deeply apologize for the inconvenience. We must abide by United States"
" laws. We hope after sanctions are lifted that we can support your "
"interest once again. Please reach out to compliance@mattermost.com for "
"any questions around current export limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:47
msgid "How do I report illicit use of Mattermost software?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:49
msgid ""
"Illicit use of Mattermost software to harm others, infringe on their "
"rights, break laws or policies is explicitly against our `Terms of Use "
"<https://mattermost.com/terms-of-use/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:51
msgid ""
"If the illicit use is happening on a web address ending in "
"``“mattermost.com”``, it means the suspected perpetrators are using "
"Mattermost software controlled by our company, Mattermost, Inc. In this "
"case, please get in touch with us at ``compliance@mattermost.com`` to "
"report the issue for us to investigate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/faq-general.rst:53
msgid ""
"If the illicit use is happening on a different web address, then it means"
" the suspected perpetrators may be using Mattermost software controlled "
"by a person or company other than Mattermost, Inc. In this case, you need"
" to contact the person or company who controls the web address by using a"
" lookup service such as https://www.whois.com/ to find the contact email "
"to report abuse. You can use a link to this FAQ as a reference to our "
"`Terms of Use <https://mattermost.com/terms-of-use/>`__ policy for "
"Mattermost software."
msgstr ""

